# Independent Patent Claim

**Claim 1:**

A flexible lighting device comprising:

a flexible substrate;

a plurality of electrically conductive traces disposed on the flexible substrate, the conductive traces configured to provide electrical power and control signals;

a plurality of flip-chip light emitting diodes (LEDs) mounted directly onto the conductive traces in electrical communication therewith, each flip-chip LED having electrical contacts on a same side as a mounting surface facing the flexible substrate, such that light emission occurs from a side opposite the mounting surface;

a transparent adhesive layer disposed over the plurality of flip-chip LEDs and at least a portion of the conductive traces; and

a transparent cover layer disposed over the transparent adhesive layer, the transparent cover layer and the transparent adhesive layer permitting transmission of light emitted from the plurality of flip-chip LEDs;

wherein the conductive traces are configured to be substantially visually imperceptible by satisfying at least one of the following conditions:

(a) the conductive traces are formed from a transparent conductive material;

(b) the conductive traces have a width of less than 300 microns; or

(c) the conductive traces are positioned beneath, aligned with, or obscured by one or more design elements disposed on or within the flexible substrate or the transparent cover layer;

such that the flexible lighting device presents a substantially uniform illuminated appearance with the conductive traces being visually imperceptible to an unaided human eye under normal viewing conditions.
